    "turn_type_label": "Substantive"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 84257,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/4/84257.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 18,
    "turn_text": "Well, I guess my question is more of a political one than a strategy, I guess, because is it worth the Democrats' time and effort to try and impeach him knowing full well that the Senate probably will not convict. Or does it behoove the Democrats to find someone they can get behind and vote the guy out of office and then prosecute him after that?",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_03",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "Impeachment by the House may not lead to conviction in the Senate.",
        "confidence": 0.96
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker views their question as primarily political rather than strategic.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "There is a possibility that the Democrats could support a candidate who would remove the individual from office through election.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "Prosecution of the individual could occur after removal from office via electoral means.",
        "confidence": 0.87
      }
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      {
        "text": "The Senate's likely lack of conviction makes impeachment a politically ineffective route for removing the individual.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "The Democratic Party values achieving political accountability even if formal impeachment fails.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "Electoral processes are a viable alternative mechanism for removing problematic officeholders.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "Democratic leadership believes in pursuing legal consequences post-office for public officials.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker assumes the Democratic Party has agency in selecting candidates for presidential elections.",
        "confidence": 0.88
      }
    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 84257,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/4/84257.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 19,
    "turn_text": "Well, obviously, the political track needs to be worked as quickly as possible. And there are obviously dozens of people now running for president. And",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
