    "turn_idx": 24,
    "turn_text": "But it shouldn't be a taboo either because we've got to think about not just this moment in history, but about the future. And if the president is engaged in high crimes and misdemeanors and offenses against the republic that really undermine the basic rule of law and our basic constitutional commitments. We have to look very seriously at that because we can't send the message to future presidents that you can use the presidency of the United States as a play thing. You can convert the U.S. government into a money-making enterprise, you can soak the whole capital in corruption and lawlessness. That's not acceptable, and we need to",
